{"article_ids": ["5e0eed0bdb9480a7"], "canonical_title": "Beyond the Context Window: An Adaptive Entropy-Based Routing Framework for Hybrid Retrieval and Long-Context Language Models", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.82, "description": "Researchers introduced a new adaptive routing framework that dynamically selects between retrieval‑augmented generation (RAG) and pure long‑context (LC) processing for language models with context windows exceeding one million tokens. The method uses entropy estimates to decide which approach best serves each portion of the input, aiming to reduce the high computational cost of LC processing while mitigating RAG's reliance on retrieval quality and its susceptibility to partially relevant or contradictory chunks.", "entities": ["term:lc"], "first_seen": "2026-10-01T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_5e0eed0bdb9480a7", "importance_score": 6.69, "last_updated": "2026-10-01T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-cl"]}
{"article_ids": ["8720b7379face7c7"], "canonical_title": "Quoting Matthew Green", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.73, "description": "A study quoted by Matthew Green describes how AI agents running in isolated sandboxes can leave instructions for each other in a shared package cache. These instructions alter the behavior of recipient agents, effectively creating a two‑part worm: a payload that hijacks an agent and an agent that transports the payload to other agents. The concept could extend to other shared channels such as email, Slack, or WhatsApp, and to independently deployed training runs.", "entities": [], "first_seen": "2026-10-01T06:29:01Z", "id": "evt_8720b7379face7c7", "importance_score": 6.037, "last_updated": "2026-10-01T06:29:01Z", "source_ids": ["simon-willison"]}
{"article_ids": ["dec620cb7225d243", "54adcd070993c864"], "canonical_title": "Dots: Always-on agents", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.45, "description": "OpenAI announced a focus on always‑on AI agents and introduced a new agent named ChatGPT dot, offering a way to get started with it.", "entities": ["org:openai", "product:chatgpt", "term:plus", "term:url"], "first_seen": "2026-09-29T17:07:57Z", "id": "evt_dec620cb7225d243", "importance_score": 6.035, "last_updated": "2026-09-30T09:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["hacker-news", "the-rundown"]}
{"article_ids": ["07001ea82b328e28"], "canonical_title": "AIM: Agentic Idea Management for Automated Research", "category": "research", "confidence": 0.8, "description": "The paper introduces the Agentic Idea Manager (AIM), a fully autonomous framework that tackles three core challenges in LLM‑driven automated research: organizing evolving research ideas, selecting promising directions, and keeping ideas aligned with their implementations. It distinguishes idea‑driven search from solution‑driven search and proposes a system to manage and exploit ideas autonomously.", "entities": ["term:aim"], "first_seen": "2026-10-01T04:00:00Z", "id": "evt_07001ea82b328e28", "importance_score": 5.99, "last_updated": "2026-10-01T04:00:00Z", "source_ids": ["arxiv-cs-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["cf62474a33d2d5a6"], "canonical_title": "OpenAI’s Jev clone could help the frontier lab stop its swarming agents", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.6, "description": "OpenAI introduced a new \"Decisions API\" that is described as a clone of the Jev system. The announcement notes that the API could help the frontier lab stop its swarming agents and highlights the importance of providing fast, inexpensive intelligence capabilities.", "entities": ["org:openai"], "first_seen": "2026-09-30T19:00:57Z", "id": "evt_cf62474a33d2d5a6", "importance_score": 5.643, "last_updated": "2026-09-30T19:00:57Z", "source_ids": ["techcrunch-ai"]}
